      "title": "`--fix` can write through an in-root symlink",
      "description": "Description: The `--fix` path passes each validated file directly to `updateFrontmatterField`, which writes to that path. The explicit-path resolver in `packages/core/src/schema/frontmatterFileValidator.ts:59-62` checks containment lexically, so a `.md` symlink inside `project-documents/user` pointing outside that directory can pass the check. Since `writeFile` follows the symlink, `cf validate frontmatter --fix` can modify an external file if it contains a fixable finding. Resolve and containment-check the real paths before allowing fixes, including files discovered by the default walk, and add a symlink-escape test.",
